{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs",
  "item": "mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Source-tool tests publish OutlineData addresses and retain mapped NodeIds\n directly in dependencies. This required Domain method is unused in\n those flows; stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs` `mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]` is a fenced commentary citation on an explicit function with a body. That is a permitted form. The commentary also gives a substantive reason rather than just difficulty.\n\nI checked each claim in the commentary against the source:\n- **`node_path` is a required `Domain` trait method.** The trait declares it in `domain.rs` `trait[Domain]/fn[node_path]`. The test fixture `Project` must therefore implement it.\n- **The source-tool tests never reach it.** The only non-test caller is `edge_fingerprint` in `graph.rs`. It is reached only for `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` and edge selections. The `Project` tests record `Dependency::Node` dependencies and run `validation::refresh_evidence`. Those tests publish `OutlineData` addresses and map them through `source_node`. Their `outgoing_edges` implementation returns an empty list, so nothing is fingerprinted. `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` ignore the node and never call `node_path`.\n- **Other domains cover `node_path`.** `tests/contracts.rs` (`identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot`, `Application`) and `tests/storage.rs` with `tests/support/stored_graph.rs` (`StoredGraph`) are separate domains that call `node_path` for stable paths and filesystem record paths.\n\nThe explanation matches the current source, so I found no gap in the citation.",
